Falsifies `system_tests::user::confined_fuzzer_tests::the_oracle_accepts_a_process_retyped_from_the_callers_own_region`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64 (the hunk is portable test-support code).

The defect it guards is the oracle's, not the kernel's: the check that decides whether a process may
fill a slot after a region retype. This patch makes the check accept every process, which is what a
careless fix for the original false positive would do. The test then fails at its first negative
case ("a space that is still held was taken as consumed"), because it hands the oracle a process
whose address space was never consumed.

A second mutation, restoring the old fill test (`self.fuzzers[x].table[s].is_none() && now[s].is_some()`),
fails the same test at the case where the process is filed in the freed space slot.

Replayed red on x86_64 on 2026-11-04 (UTC) by lane/confined-fuzzer-process-oracle.

